   "source": [
    "# Fine-tune **Gemma 3 270M** on the NHLOCAL/SingNER dataset (Kaggle, T4x2)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook converts the provided NER-style dataset (entity character spans) into an instruction-response SFT format where the model *returns the singer and album names themselves* (not positions).\n",
    "\n",
    "It then shows a practical QLoRA (4-bit via bitsandbytes) + LoRA fine-tuning flow suitable for small LLMs (Gemma 3 270M).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Notes:**\n",
    "- This recipe is designed for Kaggle Notebooks with T4 (or P100) GPUs.\n",
    "- The notebook uses `bitsandbytes` 4-bit loading (popular, memory-efficient). True Quantization-Aware-Training (QAT) into an `int4` hardware format is more advanced; a pointer to QAT resources is provided in the chat.\n",
    "- Adjust `per_device_train_batch_size`, `gradient_accumulation_steps` to your GPU RAM.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Install required packages (run once).\n",
    "# On Kaggle, you may need to restart the kernel after this cell.\n",
    "!pip install -q transformers accelerate bitsandbytes peft datasets safetensors trl huggingface_hub git+https://github.com/huggingface/trl.git"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Standard imports\n",
    "import os, json, math, random, itertools\n",
    "from datasets import load_dataset, Dataset, DatasetDict\n",
    "from transformers import AutoTokenizer, AutoConfig, AutoModelForCausalLM, BitsAndBytesConfig\n",
    "from peft import LoraConfig, get_peft_model, prepare_model_for_kbit_training\n",
    "from trl import SFTTrainer, SFTTrainingArguments\n",
    "import torch\n",
    "\n",
    "print('torch:', torch.__version__)"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Hugging Face auth (recommended) - set HUGGINGFACE_HUB_TOKEN in Kaggle Secrets or as env var.\n",
    "# os.environ['HUGGINGFACE_HUB_TOKEN'] = 'your_token_here'\n",
    "from huggingface_hub import whoami\n",
    "try:\n",
    "    print('HF Whoami:', whoami())\n",
    "except Exception as e:\n",
    "    print('not logged in to HF - set HUGGINGFACE_HUB_TOKEN if you want to push artifacts')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 1) Load the dataset from Hugging Face and inspect one example\n",
    "raw = load_dataset('NHLOCAL/SingNER')\n",
    "print(raw)\n",\    "print('Example:', raw['train'][0])\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 2) Convert NER-format (start/end/label) into SFT instruction-response pairs.\n",
    "# We will produce records: { 'input': '<instruction + text>', 'output': '<json string with singers and albums>' }\n",
    "def ner_to_sft(example):\n",
    "    text = example['text']\n",
    "    singers = []\n",
    "    albums = []\n",
    "    # dataset entities format may be a list of dicts under 'entities'\n",
    "    ents = example.get('entities', [])\n",
    "    for e in ents:\n",
    "        start = e.get('start')\n",
    "        end = e.get('end')\n",
    "        label = e.get('label')\n",
    "        if start is None or end is None:\n",
    "            continue\n",
    "        name = text[start:end]\n",
    "        if label == 'SINGER':\n",
    "            singers.append(name.strip())\n",
    "        elif label == 'ALBUM':\n",
    "            albums.append(name.strip())\n",
    "    # deduplicate while preserving order\n",
    "    def dedupe(seq):\n",
    "        seen = set(); out = []\n",
    "        for x in seq:\n",
    "            if x and x not in seen:\n",
    "                seen.add(x); out.append(x)\n",
    "        return out\n",
    "    singers = dedupe(singers)\n",
    "    albums = dedupe(albums)\n",
    "    instruction = ('Extract singer and album names from the following text. '\n",
    "                   'Return a JSON object with keys "singers" and "albums".\n\nText:\n"')\n",
    "    prompt = instruction + text + '\n\nAnswer:'\n",\    "    response = json.dumps({'singers': singers, 'albums': albums}, ensure_ascii=False)\n",
    "    return {'input': prompt, 'output': response}\n",
    "\n",
    "# Apply conversion to the whole dataset\n",
    "sft_splits = {}\n",
    "for split in raw.keys():\n",\    "    print('Converting split:', split)\n",
    "    sft_splits[split] = raw[split].map(lambda ex: ner_to_sft(ex), remove_columns=raw[split].column_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "sft = DatasetDict(sft_splits)\n",\    "print(sft)\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Quick validation of converted examples\n",
    "for i in range(3):\n",
    "    print('---')\n",
    "    print('INPUT:', sft['train'][i]['input'])\n",
    "    print('OUTPUT:', sft['train'][i]['output'])\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 3) Save converted dataset locally (optional)\n",
    "os.makedirs('data', exist_ok=True)\n",\    "sft['train'].to_json('data/train_sft.jsonl')\n",
    "if 'test' in sft:\n",
    "    sft['test'].to_json('data/valid_sft.jsonl')\n",
    "print('Saved converted dataset to data/*.jsonl')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 4) Tokenizer and model - we use the gemma 3 270M model id.\n",
    "model_name = 'google/gemma-3-270m'\n",
    "tokenizer = AutoTokenizer.from_pretrained(model_name, use_fast=False)\n",
    "# Ensure tokenizer has pad token\n",
    "if tokenizer.pad_token is None:\n",
    "    tokenizer.add_special_tokens({'pad_token': '[PAD]'})\n",\    "print('Tokenizer loaded. Vocab size:', len(tokenizer))\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 5) Prepare model loading in 4-bit via bitsandbytes (QLoRA style).\n",
    "bnb_config = BitsAndBytesConfig(
    "    load_in_4bit=True,
    "    bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.float16,
    "    bnb_4bit_use_double_quant=True,
    "    bnb_4bit_quant_type='nf4'
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Preparing model in 4-bit. This reduces memory and is recommended for small GPUs like T4.')\n",
    "# For kbit training preparation (peft / qlora), we call prepare_model_for_kbit_training\n",
    "config = AutoConfig.from_pretrained(model_name)\n",
    "model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(
    "    model_name,
    "    device_map='auto',
    "    quantization_config=bnb_config,
    "    trust_remote_code=True
    " )\n",
    "model = prepare_model_for_kbit_training(model)\n",
    "print('Model loaded.')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 6) Set up LoRA (PEFT) adapters\n",
    "lora_config = LoraConfig(
    "    r=8,
    "    lora_alpha=32,
    "    target_modules=['q_proj','v_proj','k_proj','o_proj','gate_proj','down_proj','up_proj'],
    "    lora_dropout=0.05,
    "    bias='none',
    "    task_type='CAUSAL_LM'
    " )\n",
    "model = get_peft_model(model, lora_config)\n",
    "print('LoRA adapters attached.')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 7) Prepare tokenized dataset for SFTTrainer\n",
    "max_length = 512\n",
    "def tokenize_fn(example):\n",
    "    prompt = example['input']\n",
    "    response = example['output']\n",
    "    # full text: prompt + response for causal LM; you may add special tokens if desired\n",
    "    full = prompt + ' ' + response\n",
    "    toks = tokenizer(full, truncation=True, max_length=max_length, padding='max_length')\n",
    "    return {'input_ids': toks['input_ids'], 'attention_mask': toks['attention_mask']}\n",
    "\n",
    "train_tok = sft['train'].map(tokenize_fn, remove_columns=sft['train'].column_names)
",
    "valid_tok = None\n",
    "if 'test' in sft:\n",
    "    valid_tok = sft['test'].map(tokenize_fn, remove_columns=sft['test'].column_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Tokenized dataset: train size =', len(train_tok))\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 8) SFT Training arguments and trainer setup\n",
    "training_args = SFTTrainingArguments(
    "    output_dir='outputs/gemma3-lora',
    "    per_device_train_batch_size=1,
    "    gradient_accumulation_steps=16,
    "    num_train_epochs=3,
    "    learning_rate=2e-4,
    "    fp16=True,
    "    logging_steps=20,
    "    save_strategy='epoch',
    "    remove_unused_columns=False,
    "    save_total_limit=2,
    " )\n",
    "trainer = SFTTrainer(
    "    model=model,
    "    args=training_args,
    "    train_dataset=train_tok,
    "    eval_dataset=valid_tok if valid_tok is not None else None,
    "    tokenizer=tokenizer,
    " )\n",
    "\n",
    "# NOTE: Depending on your Kaggle quota and GPU memory you may need to lower gradient_accumulation_steps or num_train_epochs\n",
    "print('Trainer prepared.')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 9) Run training (this will start the fine-tuning)\n",
    "trainer.train()\n",
    "trainer.save_model('outputs/gemma3-lora-final')\n",
    "print('Training finished and adapter saved.')\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 10) Inference example using the tuned model\n",
    "from transformers import pipeline\n",
    "# Load the model with adapters (we assume device_map='auto' to pick GPU)\n",
    "model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained('outputs/gemma3-lora-final', device_map='auto')\n",
    "pipe = pipeline('text-generation', model=model, tokenizer=tokenizer, device=0)\n",
    "prompt = 'Extract singer and album names from the following text.\n\nText:\nמרום שטיינברג אילי מנצל רון קירשנבוים - עברתי בחושך (קולולחן)\n\nAnswer:'\n",
    "print(pipe(prompt, max_new_tokens=128))\n"
   ],
   "execution_count": null,
   "outputs": []
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "---\n",
    "## Advanced: Notes about QAT (int4) vs QLoRA (bitsandbytes 4-bit)\n",
    "- The notebook uses *bitsandbytes* 4-bit loading (nf4) + LoRA (QLoRA style). That is the practical and widely-used approach for memory-limited GPUs (T4).\n",
    "- True Quantization-Aware Training (QAT) targeted at int4 hardware formats (and special GGUF conversions) exists but usually requires more advanced frameworks or manual insertion of fake-quant modules. See PyTorch's QAT guide and Google Gemma QLoRA docs for more.\n",
    "\n",
    "If you need a true QAT -> int4 pipeline (research-level), I included up-to-date pointers in the chat message accompanying this notebook.\n"
   ]
  }
 ]
}
